Yes, I believe fast food consumption is a significant contributor to the global obesity epidemic. 

The evidence is pretty compelling. Fast food is often high in calories, unhealthy fats, sugar, and sodium, while being low in essential nutrients. Regularly consuming these types of foods can lead to weight gain and increase the risk of developing obesity-related health problems like heart disease, type 2 diabetes, and certain cancers. 

While individual choices play a role, the widespread availability and aggressive marketing of fast food, particularly targeting vulnerable populations, makes it a major factor in the global obesity crisis.  We need to be honest about the impact of these food choices on our health and work towards promoting healthier alternatives.<end_of_turn>
