I firmly believe Compulsive Buying Disorder is best addressed through medical treatment.  While personal responsibility is important in all aspects of life,  this disorder goes beyond simple willpower. It's a complex mental health condition with neurological underpinnings.  

Treating it as solely a matter of personal responsibility ignores the underlying biological and psychological factors at play.  It's like telling someone with diabetes to just "eat less sugar" – it oversimplifies a complex issue. 

Medical treatment, including therapy and in some cases medication, can help individuals understand the root causes of their compulsive buying, develop coping mechanisms, and manage the urges that drive this behavior.  It's about providing the tools and support necessary to address the disorder effectively.<end_of_turn>
